## 5. Execution Phases

### Phase 0 — Pre-flight

1. Confirm the target session exists: `opencode session list | grep {{SESSION_ID}}`.
2. Confirm the gap-closure gate in section 4 is cleared.
3. If this plan is already retired, recover it from the OS Trash by exact filename.
4. Verify every content marker in section 2 against the CURRENT working tree,
   using the listed command. Record `git status --short` for every marker file.
   STOP if any marker is missing or if no marker baseline exists.
5. Run the deletion composer's dry-run and compare its inventory with section 1.

### Phase 1 — Delete

```bash
python3 .agents/skills/opencode/session/opencode-session-deletion/scripts/delete-session.py {{SESSION_ID}} --execute --gap-closure-cleared
```

### Phase 2 — Verify and recreation guard

1. Confirm no database record, log path, or scratch path remains.
2. Wait about 10 seconds and re-run the same checks; if anything reappears,
   close the target TUI and repeat.

### Phase 3 — Retire this plan last

```bash
trash "<absolute-path-of-this-plan>"
```

